  "id": "acculturation-strategies",
  "term": "acculturation strategies",
  "definition": "Acculturation strategies are the main ways people adapt when living between a home culture and a receiving culture. They describe whether a person mainly keeps their culture of origin, mainly adopts the host culture, does both, or does neither.",
